Subject: Weekly Campaign Performance Update (June 1–7)

Hi Team,
Sharing a quick performance update for the week of June 1–7.

Overall delivery increased this week, with impressions rising by 18% after the budget ramp-up. Clicks dipped by 6%, which resulted in a CTR decline from 2.4% to 1.9%. Conversions remained stable at 152, and CPC increased slightly by around 4%.

From the data, the CTR drop appears to be linked to two main factors. First, the new audience segment introduced this week is generating higher volume but lower engagement. Second, a larger share of delivery shifted toward mobile app placements, which historically perform below average for this campaign. Despite these shifts, conversion quality remains consistent, which is a positive sign.

To stabilize performance, I recommend reducing spend on the low-CTR audience segment and refreshing the top creatives, as they have been running for over five weeks. It would also help to shift delivery back toward high-performing feed placements. These adjustments should help recover CTR over the coming days.

